{
  "id": "80571",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Selective Precipitation",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Because of their light sensitivity, mixtures of silver halides are used in fiber optics for medical lasers, in photochromic eyeglass lenses (glass lenses that automatically darken when exposed to sunlight), and—before the advent of digital photography—in photographic film. Even though AgCl ("
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "sp"
              },
              {
                "text": " = 1.6 × 10"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "–10"
              },
              {
                "text": "), AgBr ("
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "sp"
              },
              {
                "text": " = 5.0 × 10"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "–13"
              },
              {
                "text": "), and AgI ("
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "sp"
              },
              {
                "text": " = 1.5 × 10"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "–16"
              },
              {
                "text": "), are each quite insoluble, we cannot prepare a homogeneous solid mixture of them by adding Ag"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "+"
              },
              {
                "text": " to a solution of Cl"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "–"
              },
              {
                "text": ", Br"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "–"
              },
              {
                "text": ", and I"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "–"
              },
              {
                "text": ". Essentially all of the AgI will precipitate before any of the other solid halides form because of its smaller value for "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "sp"
              },
              {
                "text": ". However, we can prepare a "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "homogeneous mixture"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "A mixture that has a uniform composition and appears visually the same throughout."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "3641945070",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "794126143",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": " of the solids by slowly adding a solution of Cl"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "–"
              },
              {
                "text": ", Br"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "–"
              },
              {
                "text": ", and I"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "–"
              },
              {
                "text": " to a solution of Ag"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "+"
              },
              {
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            "id": "4dghbkpiy79c2vl",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "When two anions form slightly soluble compounds with the same cation, or when two cations form slightly soluble compounds with the same anion, the less soluble compound (usually the compound with the smaller "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "sp"
              },
              {
                "text": ") generally precipitates first when we add a precipitating agent to a solution containing both anions (or both cations). When the "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "sp"
              },
              {
                "text": " values of the two compounds differ by two orders of magnitude or more (e.g., 10"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "–2"
              },
              {
                "text": " vs. 10"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "–4"
              },
              {
                "text": "), almost all of the less soluble compound precipitates before any of the more soluble one does. This is an example of "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "selective precipitation"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "A technique for separating ions in an aqueous solution using differences in their solubility with a given precipitating reagent."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "4139396839",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1378025664",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": ", where a reagent is added to a solution of dissolved ions, causing one of the ions to precipitate out before the rest."
              }
            ],
            "id": "wqizx8d7zcogqoj",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Selective precipitation can also be used in qualitative analysis. In this method, reagents are added to an unknown chemical mixture to induce precipitation. Certain reagents cause specific ions to precipitate out; therefore, the addition of the reagent can be used to determine whether the ion is present in the solution."
              }
            ],
            "id": "ptsb7eueh08qhex",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "4282368998",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "A solution contains 0.0010 mol of KI and 0.10 mol of KCl per liter. AgNO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is gradually added to this solution. Which forms first, solid AgI or solid AgCl?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "sg9s19wr8almlld",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The two equilibria involved are:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "ue2irvhhbjkwmn0",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "1uugcpdtzg20blc",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "ljqvfmgln1jo5aj",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\begin{array}{l}\\mathrm{AgCl}(s)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;\\mathrm{Ag}^+(aq)\\;+\\;\\mathrm{Cl}^-(aq)\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;K_{\\mathrm{sp}}\\;=\\;1.6\\times10^{-10}\\;\\;\\;\\\\\\mathrm{AgI}(s)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;\\mathrm{Ag}^+(aq)\\;+\\;\\mathrm I^-(aq)\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;K_{\\mathrm{sp}}\\;=\\;1.5\\times10^{-16}\\end{array}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "If the solution contained about equal concentrations of Cl"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "–"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and I"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "–"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", then the silver salt with the smallest "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "K"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "sp"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " (AgI) would precipitate first. The concentrations are not equal, however, so we should find the [Ag"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] at which AgCl begins to precipitate and the [Ag"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] at which AgI begins to precipitate. The salt that forms at the lower [Ag"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] precipitates first."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "xs67iigb0lenjvk",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "For AgI:"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " AgI precipitates when "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "Q"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " equals "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "K"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "sp"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " for AgI (1.5 × 10"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−16"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "). When [I"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "–"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] = 0.0010 M:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "rzt2cx48gk71zb1",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "4c0fdw1nrbmdxq0",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "bsu8rj9qu5iv7cc",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\begin{array}{l}Q\\;=\\;\\lbrack\\mathrm{Ag}^+\\rbrack\\lbrack\\mathrm I^-\\rbrack\\;=\\;\\lbrack\\mathrm{Ag}^+\\rbrack(0.0010)\\; =\\;1.5\\times10^{-16}\\;\\;\\;\\;\\\\\\\\\\lbrack\\mathrm{Ag}^+\\rbrack\\;=\\;\\frac{1.5\\times10^{-16}}{0.0010}\\; =\\;1.5\\times10^{-13}\\;\\mathrm M\\end{array}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "AgI begins to precipitate when [Ag"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] is 1.5 × 10"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "–13"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " M."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "eljyimsdl7x6sbg",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "For AgCl:"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " AgCl precipitates when "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "Q"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " equals "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "K"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "sp"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " for AgCl (1.6 × 10"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "–10"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "). When [Cl"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "–"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] = 0.10 M:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "hkxr9u1nac9lg20",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "lkfwqtj6r2m2yyg",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "ps2ng4e0cmpa55p",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\begin{array}{l}Q\\;=\\;\\lbrack\\mathrm{Ag}^+\\rbrack\\lbrack\\mathrm{Cl}^-\\rbrack\\;=\\;\\lbrack\\mathrm{Ag}^+\\rbrack(0.10)\\; =\\;1.6\\times10^{-10}\\;\\;\\;\\;\\\\\\\\\\lbrack\\mathrm{Ag}^+\\rbrack\\;=\\;\\frac{1.6\\times10^{-10}}{0.10}\\; =\\;1.6\\times10^{-9}\\;\\mathrm M\\end{array}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": " AgCl begins to precipitate when [Ag"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] is 1.6 × 10"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "–9"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " M."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2vazl7yyjmlywhv",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "AgI begins to precipitate at a lower [Ag"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] than AgCl, so AgI begins to precipitate first. "
                  }
                ],
                "id": "932vvt6izi9dc6t",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "id": "3227929947",
